    <statement><p>Find the speed at the given value of t:</p>
<p><m>{\bf r\it(t)} = \left\lt e^{t-7},7,7 t^{-1}\right&gt; , t=7</m></p>
<p><m>v(7)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.01015</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\left\lt e^{t-7},0,-7 t^{-2}\right&gt;</m> and at 
<m>t=7</m>
<me>\bf r\it'(7)=\left\lt  e^{7-7},0,-7\cdot 7^{-2} \right&gt; = \left\lt 1,0,-\frac{1}{7}\right&gt;.</me>
The speed is the magnitude of the velocity vector, that is,
<me>v(7)=\|\bf r\it'(7)\|=\sqrt{1^2+0^2+\left(-\frac{1}{7}\right)^2}=\sqrt{\frac{50}{49}}
\approx 1.01</me>


</solution>
